1
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
The Man... The Music... The Madness... The Murder... The Motion Picture.

2
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Amadeus is a history, music, drama film directed by Miloš Forman.

3
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Disciplined Italian composer Antonio Salieri becomes consumed by jealousy and resentment towards the
hedonistic and remarkably talented young Salzburger composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.

4
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Antonio Salieri, played by F. Murray Abraham.

5
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, played by Tom Hulce.

6
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Constanze Mozart, played by Elizabeth Berridge.

7
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Emanuel Schikaneder, played by Simon Callow.

8
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Leopold Mozart, played by Roy Dotrice.

9
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Katerina Cavalieri, played by Christine Ebersole.

10
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Amadeus is a 1984 American period drama film directed by Miloš Forman.

11
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Peter Shaffer adapted it from his 1979 stage play, inspired by
Alexander Pushkin's 1830 play Mozart and Salieri.

12
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Shaffer described it as a "fantasia on [a real-life] theme", as it imagines a rivalry between two
18th-century Vienna composers, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart (Tom Hulce) and Antonio Salieri (F.

13
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Murray Abraham).

14
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Salieri struggles to reconcile his professional admiration and jealous hatred for Mozart,
and resolves to ruin Mozart's career as his form of vengeance against God.

15
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Amadeus received its world premiere in Los Angeles on September 6, 1984.

16
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
It was released by Orion Pictures thirteen days later to widespread critical
acclaim and box office success, grossing over $90 million.

17
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
It was nominated for 53 awards and won 40, including 8 Academy Awards (including Best Picture), four
BAFTA Awards, and four Golden Globe Awards (including Best Motion Picture – Drama).

18
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
Abraham and Hulce were both nominated for the Academy
Award for Best Actor, with Abraham winning.

19
02:06:40,000 --> 02:06:46,000
In 1998, the American Film Institute ranked it 53rd on its 100 Years...

20
02:13:20,000 --> 02:13:26,000
100 Movies list.

21
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
In 2019, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

22
02:26:40,000 --> 02:26:46,000
The film explores themes of opera, composer, musician, marriage crisis, italy.

23
02:33:20,000 --> 02:33:26,000
The tone is emotional.
